0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 731 Td (Imagine a small office that opens new customer accounts. A visitor submits a form. A) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 717 Td (receptionist checks that it is filled out correctly, a clerk handles the request, a policy) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 703 Td (desk checks the rules, a records desk talks to the database, and the office returns a result.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 686 Td (In this app, those roles are separated into code folders. Each part has one main) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 672 Td (responsibility. The separation makes it easier to understand, test, and change the system.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 650 Td (The registration request journey) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 627 Td (- A client sends HTTP POST /auth/register with JSON account details.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 611 Td (- Express parses the JSON body in app.ts.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 595 Td (- The auth router matches /register, because app.ts mounted that router under /auth.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 579 Td (- Validation middleware checks the request against registerSchema.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
