BT /F1 20 Tf 54 765 Td (3. Foundations: common programming words) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 726 Td (Values and data types) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 703 Td (- string: text, such as an email or a person's name.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 687 Td (- number: a numeric value, such as 7000 or an HTTP status code.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 671 Td (- boolean: true or false, such as whether an email was found.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 655 Td (- object: named values grouped together, such as { name, email }.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 639 Td (- array: an ordered list of values, such as rows returned by a database query.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 623 Td (- undefined: no value was found or assigned. A lookup can return undefined when there is no) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 609 Td (- matching user.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 62 593 Td (- null: an explicitly empty value. It is different from undefined.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 572 Td (Variables, constants, and names) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 549 Td (const creates a variable binding that cannot be reassigned. The object it points to might) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 535 Td (still be mutable, but simple values such as a string cannot be reassigned to that const name.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 521 Td (Names like input, userRepository, and passwordHash are names chosen by the programmer; they) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 507 Td (are not special words.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 485 Td (Functions, parameters, and returns) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 462 Td (A function is a reusable set of steps. A parameter is an input to that function. return sends) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 448 Td (a result back to its caller and stops that function. Example: signUpService\(input\) receives) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 434 Td (signup fields; return sends a success or error result to the controller.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 412 Td (Classes and instances) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 389 Td (A class groups related methods and describes how to make an object. UserRepository is a class.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 375 Td (new UserRepository\(\) makes an instance that the service can use, like taking a working copy of) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 361 Td (the records-desk toolkit.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 339 Td (Async and await) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 316 Td (A database or password hash takes time. async marks a function that can perform asynchronous) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 302 Td (work. await pauses that function until the work finishes, without freezing the whole server.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 288 Td (The result becomes available after the wait.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 266 Td (Imports and exports) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 243 Td (An import brings a value or type from another package/file into the current file. An export) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 229 Td (makes something available for other files to import. Like borrowing a tool from another room) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 215 Td (and labeling a tool for others to use.) Tj ET
0.12 0.22 0.34 rg
BT /F2 8.1 Tf 64 198 Td (import { z } from "zod";) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 185 Td (The braces mean a named export is being selected. In this example, the Zod package exports a) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 171 Td (named value called z. z is Zod's main API object: it provides tools such as z.object\(\),) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 157 Td (z.string\(\), and z.email\(\). It is not a TypeScript keyword and it was not invented in this) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 143 Td (file. The package was installed as a project dependency.) Tj ET
0.12 0.22 0.34 rg
BT /F2 8.1 Tf 64 126 Td (import type { Request, Response } from "express";) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 113 Td (The word type means these imports are only needed by TypeScript to check types. They are not) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 54 99 Td (runtime objects the app has to call.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 13 Tf 54 77 Td (Types are not runtime validation) Tj ET
